LoadRaw: one read per window.
The function asks for count + 1 bars, not count, because row 0 needs the previous bar's close for its return and the previous bar's ATR as its yardstick. Both arrays are non-series, so index 0 is the oldest bar, which is also the order the matrix rows are built in. If either CopyRates or CopyBuffer returns fewer bars than requested, the whole call fails and the caller simply tries again on the next bar. A half-filled window would fit a scaler to partial data, which is worse than no verdict at all. A non-positive price or ATR also aborts the load, since the log and the division would be undefined.
//+------------------------------------------------------------------+
//| CMarketFeatures::LoadRaw                                         |
//| Builds 'count' raw feature rows, oldest first, where the newest  |
//| row belongs to the bar at 'first_shift' (1 = last closed bar).   |
//|                                                                  |
//| One extra older bar is read. Row 0 needs the previous close for  |
//| its return and the previous bar's ATR as the volatility          |
//| yardstick, so the range is measured against conditions that      |
//| existed BEFORE the bar formed. Returns false on any short read.  |
