These two helpers are the formulas from the architecture section, written once and used for both reference points and new queries. They take an offset into the neighbour arrays, so a reference point can read its neighbours from row * k in the flat tables while a query reads them from the start of two small local arrays.
//+------------------------------------------------------------------+
//| CLOFEngine::LocalReachDensity                                    |
//| Computes lrd = 1 / (mean reachability distance + LOF_EPS) for    |
//| one point whose neighbours start at 'offset' inside idx[] and    |
//| val[].                                                           |
//|                                                                  |
//| The reachability distance from the point to neighbour o is       |
//| max(k-distance(o), d(point, o)). Using the neighbour's own       |
//| k-distance as a floor smooths the estimate: points inside a      |
//| tight cluster all 'reach' each other at the cluster's typical    |
//| spacing instead of at their tiny raw distances.                  |
