LOF_Gate_EA.mq5: The Entry Gate
The EA is a deliberately plain strategy with the gate applied. When the 20-period EMA crosses the 50-period EMA on a closed bar, it opens a market position with a stop loss two ATRs away and a take profit three ATRs away. An opposite cross closes the position. The LOF gate has exactly one power: it can veto a new entry. It never closes a trade, never changes the size and, unless the optional tightening is switched on, never touches a stop. That keeps the comparison clean. With InpUseGate set to false the EA is the plain crossover, and with it set to true the only difference between the two runs is the set of vetoed signals.
The inputs come in three groups: the base strategy, the LOF gate, and an optional stop-tightening mode that is switched off in every test in this article. The defaults are the values used throughout the testing section.
