OnTick: the order of decisions.
Intra-bar ticks carry no new information for a model that reads closed bars, so the handler returns immediately unless a new bar has opened. LOF is refreshed only when something depends on it, which keeps the ungated baseline run fast. An opposite cross closes the current position first, and closing is never blocked by the gate. Only after that does the veto run: if the bar just scored is flagged, the signal is dropped and a counter is incremented.
